\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Means on equal blocks}
\date{2026-11-06}

\p{Split the vertices of the circle mesh into an integer number
of contiguous blocks of equal size, and replace the field on
each block by the mean of its values. The mesh precision
couples only neighboring vertices. When the blocks are
refined, do these means keep a precision supported on
neighboring blocks, and do their covariances agree with
averages of the Green function in \ref{fdip-00BG}?}
